    "text": "Elatha, also known as Elada, Eladha, or Elotha, was an Irish hero. He was among the few beautiful Fomorians, the early residents of Ireland. His name means 'craft' or 'skill.' He mated with the land goddess Ériu, whose people, the Tuatha Dé Danann, displaced the Fomorians. He gave Ériu a golden ring and prophesied a son, Bres mac Elatha. Bres, half-Fomorian, proved a stingy and unreliable king. His rule led to the battle of Mag Tuired.",
